      "worked": "Domain:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-1&>0\\\\x&>\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nVertical asymptote:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-1&=0\\\\x&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $x$-intercept, set $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1-\\ln(2x-1)&=0\\\\\\ln(2x-1)&=1\\\\2x-1&=e\\\\x&=\\frac{e+1}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nThere is no $y$-intercept because $0$ is outside the domain. The range is $(-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nAs $x$ approaches $\\frac12$ from the right, $y$ approaches $\\infty$. As $x$ increases without bound, $y$ approaches $-\\infty$. Draw a decreasing logarithmic curve through $\\left(\\frac{e+1}{2},0\\right)$.",
